                "community_notes": null,
                "conversation_id": "1975991101007003809",
                "created_time": "2025-10-08T18:26:05",
                "favorite_count": 1,
                "geo_lat": null,
                "geo_lon": null,
                "id": "1975991101007003809",
                "in_reply_to_post_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_username": null,
                "place_country_code": null,
                "place_country_name": null,
                "place_full_name": null,
                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "post",
                "quote_count": 0,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 3,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "In my district, everyone will see their healthcare costs rise under Republicans\u2019 extreme healthcare plans \u2014 but for the 22,000 people who rely on the Affordable Care Act marketplace, the increase would be devastating.\u00a0\n\u00a0\nAlongside my Democratic colleagues, I\u2019m fighting to protect affordable healthcare for families in the Valley and across the nation.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1759947965,
                "view_count": 213
            },
            {
                "attached_links_expanded_url": null,
                "attached_links_url": null,
                "attached_medias_preview_url": null,
                "attached_medias_url": null,
                "attached_videos": null,
                "author_id": "245451804",
                "author_username": "RepJimCosta",
                "community_notes": null,
                "conversation_id": "1976040794642579499",
                "created_time": "2025-10-08T21:43:33",
                "favorite_count": 3,
                "geo_lat": null,
                "geo_lon": null,
                "id": "1976040794642579499",
                "in_reply_to_post_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_username": null,
                "place_country_code": null,
                "place_country_name": null,
                "place_full_name": null,
                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "post",
                "quote_count": 0,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "In July, Republicans passed the \"Big Beautiful Bill\", slashing over $1 trillion from Medicaid, CHIP, and the Affordable Care Act. Now, they\u2019re pushing another bill that would raise ACA premium tax credits, adding yet another cost burden on working families.\n \nHere in CA-21, that means:\n\u274c65,000 residents will lose their Medicaid coverage.\n\u274c22,000 people who rely on the ACA marketplace would face devastating premium hikes. \n \nHealth care is a right, not a privilege. I\u2019ll keep fighting to protect affordable, quality care for every family in the Valley.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1759959813,
                "view_count": 339
            },
            {
                "attached_links_expanded_url": null,
                "attached_links_url": null,
                "attached_medias_preview_url": null,
                "attached_medias_url": null,
                "attached_videos": null,
                "author_id": "245451804",
                "author_username": "RepJimCosta",
                "community_notes": null,
                "conversation_id": "1978219313178780154",
                "created_time": "2025-10-14T22:00:12",
                "favorite_count": 0,
                "geo_lat": null,
                "geo_lon": null,
                "id": "1978219313178780154",
                "in_reply_to_post_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_username": null,
                "place_country_code": null,
                "place_country_name": null,
                "place_full_name": null,
                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "post",
                "quote_count": 0,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Buffer",
                "text": "Today marks day 14 of the government shutdown. My Democratic colleagues and I are fighting to protect healthcare for hardworking families, including those here in the Valley. \n\nIf these vital tax credits aren\u2019t extended, 22,000 people in my district will see their healthcare costs go up. That\u2019s unacceptable and just plain wrong.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1760479212,
                "view_count": 214
            },
            {
                "attached_links_expanded_url": null,
                "attached_links_url": null,
                "attached_medias_preview_url": null,
                "attached_medias_url": null,
                "attached_videos": null,
                "author_id": "245451804",
                "author_username": "RepJimCosta",
                "community_notes": null,
                "conversation_id": "1978249511056155090",
                "created_time": "2025-10-15T00:00:12",
                "favorite_count": 0,
                "geo_lat": null,
                "geo_lon": null,
                "id": "1978249511056155090",
                "in_reply_to_post_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_username": null,
                "place_country_code": null,
                "place_country_name": null,
                "place_full_name": null,
                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "post",
                "quote_count": 0,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 0,
                "source": "Buffer",
                "text": "Families in CA-21 can\u2019t afford higher health care costs. If Republicans let critical tax credits expire, a family of four earning $64,000 could see their premiums rise by over $2,500 a year. \n\nWe need a bipartisan solution. It\u2019s time to come to the table and make healthcare affordable for all Americans.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1760486412,
                "view_count": 231
            },
            {
                "attached_links_expanded_url": null,
                "attached_links_url": null,
                "attached_medias_preview_url": null,
                "attached_medias_url": null,
                "attached_videos": null,
                "author_id": "245451804",
                "author_username": "RepJimCosta",
                "community_notes": null,
                "conversation_id": "1980304404956811356",
                "created_time": "2025-10-20T16:05:37",
                "favorite_count": 3,
                "geo_lat": null,
                "geo_lon": null,
                "id": "1980304404956811356",
                "in_reply_to_post_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_id": null,
                "in_reply_to_profile_username": null,
                "place_country_code": null,
                "place_country_name": null,
                "place_full_name": null,
                "place_type": null,
                "poll": null,
                "post_type": "post",
                "quote_count": 0,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Buffer",
                "text": "Hardworking Valley families are about to face skyrocketing health care costs. It\u2019s time for House Republicans to work across the aisle, reopen the government, and stop these premium hikes.\n\nTheir reckless \u201cBig Ugly Bill\u201d has created a health care crisis\u2014slashing Medicaid, forcing hospitals and health centers to close, and now driving premiums even higher.",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1760976337,
                "view_count": 280
            },
